From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Show the firmware's own power state
 in debugfs

The M4 GPU never powers down at an idle desktop, while macOS keeps it
off almost all of the time. The firmware decides that by itself: its
power state machine (the idle decision, the idle timer, the deferral of
a power-down while the host is kicking, the power-down itself) keeps
its state in objects the host allocated, mainly POWER_PERFORMANCE (the
one Runtime +0x469 points at) and POWER (root +0xb8). Nothing of ours
reads them, so on the device it cannot be told whether the firmware
never takes the idle decision, takes it and defers forever, or powers
down while the domain stays up.

Add aurora-g16/fwpower, one line per read with the firmware's power
state, its idle sub-state, the deferral flag and counters, the current
performance state, the root.Control status words and the Globals words
the firmware checks before a power-down. The file holds its own
references to the four objects and reads them without the device lock,
so it can be sampled quickly around a burst of work without stalling
submission. Nothing is written; the firmware cannot see the reads.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/initdata.rs | 12 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/mod.rs      |  4 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/poll.rs     | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 82 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/initdata.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/initdata.rs
index 06d7ee1aae..c8c9b5a955 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/initdata.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/initdata.rs
@@ -67,6 +67,18 @@ pub(crate) fn halted(&self) -> Result<bool> {
         Ok(phase == 1 || phase == 3)
     }
 
+    /// The objects behind `aurora-g16/fwpower`: POWER_PERFORMANCE, POWER, the small
+    /// root.Control and Globals, in that order. Shared references; nothing is copied.
+    pub(crate) fn fwpower_objects(&self) -> Option<[Arc<FwObject>; 4]> {
+        let graph = |i: usize| self._graph.get(i).cloned();
+        Some([
+            graph(id::POWER_PERFORMANCE)?,
+            graph(id::POWER)?,
+            self.ready_control.clone()?,
+            self.globals.clone()?,
+        ])
+    }
+
     /// Firmware's actual READY acknowledgement in the small root.Control object.
     pub(crate) fn readiness(&self) -> Result<u32> {
         self.ready_control
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/mod.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/mod.rs
index 5bab8907fc..adac5cb372 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/mod.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/mod.rs
